    watsonx Orchestrate	

        Required if you run models locally.
        Not required if you use the AI gateway to access third-party models.

About this task

All of the services that require GPUs require the NVIDIA GPU Operator and the Node Feature Discovery Operator.
Review the following table to determine which operators you need to upgrade:
Operator
	
Upgrade this operator if...
Node Feature Discovery Operator	

You upgraded Red Hat OpenShift® Container Platform and the operator is installed with installPlanApproval: Manual.
NVIDIA GPU Operator	

The version of the operator on your cluster has reached the end of support. For details, see NVIDIA GPU Operator Life Cycle in the
Procedure

    To upgrade the Node Feature Discovery Operator, follow the appropriate steps for your environment:
        To upgrade the operator on a cluster that can connect to the internet, complete Installing the Node Feature Discovery OperatorNode Feature Discovery (NFD) in the NVIDIA GPU Operator on Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform documentation.
        To upgrade the operator on a cluster that is disconnected or air-gapped, complete Deploy GPU Operators in a disconnected or air-gapped environment in the NVIDIA GPU Operator on Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform documentation.
    To upgrade the NVIDIA GPU Operator, follow the appropriate steps for your environment:
        To upgrade the operator on a cluster that can connect to the internet, complete Installing the NVIDIA GPU Operator in the NVIDIA GPU Operator on Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform documentation.
        To upgrade the operator on a cluster that is disconnected or air-gapped, complete Deploy GPU Operators in a disconnected or air-gapped environment in the NVIDIA GPU Operator on Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform documentation.

What to do next

Now that you've upgraded the operators for services that require GPUs, you're ready to complete Upgrading Red Hat OpenShift AI (Upgrading from Version 5.1 to Version 5.3).
